        <h2>Laid down one block per cycle</h2>
        <div class="grid3">
    <article class="card" data-growth="1"><h3>Middle-out, in one sentence</h3><p>Start from N independent midpoints and expand outward, so no segment waits on another. Parallel by construction, lossless by geometry.</p></article>
        <article class="card" data-growth="2"><h3>Weissman score</h3><p>The show's fictional benchmark: effective compression over a theoretical baseline. Pied Piper's 5.2 made grown engineers weep. This site's ticker still oscillates 5.1–5.4 in tribute.</p></article>
        <article class="card" data-growth="3" data-seed="0"><h3>The workstation: CodeEditor.tsx</h3><p>Pasted four times, grown once — deduplicated. 16 quick-insert symbols, synced line numbers, cursor tracking, Tab handling, touch-aware focus. Committed verbatim at CodeEditor.tsx and opened live in the site editor. This block grew from a planted seed, not the built-in dozen.</p></article>
        <article class="card" data-growth="4"><h3>XOR deltas</h3><p>Inside each segment, every word is stored as curr ^ prev. Structured data yields sparse, mostly-zero diffs — and sparse diffs compress.</p></article>
        <article class="card" data-growth="5" data-seed="1"><h3>Learn track: HTML foundations</h3><p>Start https://www.w3schools.com/html/default.asp — intro https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_intro.asp — editors https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_editors.asp — basic https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_basic.asp — elements https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_elements.asp — attributes https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_attributes.asp — practice https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_exercises.asp and https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_quiz.asp</p></article>
        <article class="card" data-growth="6" data-seed="2"><h3>Learn track: HTML text and style</h3><p>Headings https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_headings.asp — paragraphs https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_paragraphs.asp — styles https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_styles.asp — formatting https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_formatting.asp — quotations https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_quotation_elements.asp — comments https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_comments.asp — colors https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_colors.asp<details><summary>working example — HTML forms (from https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_forms.asp)</summary><pre><code>&lt;form&gt;
  &lt;label for="fname"&gt;First name:&lt;/label&gt;&lt;br&gt;
  &lt;input type="text" id="fname" name="fname"&gt;&lt;br&gt;
  &lt;label for="lname"&gt;Last name:&lt;/label&gt;&lt;br&gt;
  &lt;input type="text" id="lname" name="lname"&gt;
&lt;/form&gt;</code></pre><ul><li>label for must equal input id to bind them</li><li>every submittable input needs a name attribute or its value is never sent</li><li>one shared radio name means one choice</li><li>form action points at the server-side handler</li></ul></details></p></article>
        <article class="card" data-growth="7" data-seed="3"><h3>Learn track: HTML structure</h3><p>Links https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_links.asp — images https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_images.asp — tables https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_tables.asp — lists https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_lists.asp — blocks https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_blocks.asp — div https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_div.asp — classes https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_classes.asp — id https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_id.asp<details><summary>working example — HTML tables (from https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_tables.asp)</summary><pre><code>&lt;table&gt;
  &lt;tr&gt;
    &lt;th&gt;Company&lt;/th&gt;
    &lt;th&gt;Contact&lt;/th&gt;
    &lt;th&gt;Country&lt;/th&gt;
  &lt;/tr&gt;
  &lt;tr&gt;
    &lt;td&gt;Alfreds Futterkiste&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td&gt;Maria Anders&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td&gt;Germany&lt;/td&gt;
  &lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;</code></pre><ul><li>td is data, tr is row, th is header (bold and centered by default)</li><li>keep the same cell count in each row</li><li>a cell can hold text, images, lists, links, even other tables</li></ul></details></p></article>
        <article class="card" data-growth="8" data-seed="4"><h3>Learn track: HTML forms and pages</h3><p>Forms https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_forms.asp — form attributes https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_forms_attributes.asp — form elements https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_form_elements.asp — input types https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_form_input_types.asp — head https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_head.asp — layout https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_layout.asp — responsive https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_responsive.asp — semantics https://www.w3schools.com/html/html5_semantic_elements.asp — favicon https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_favicon.asp — page title https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_page_title.asp<details><summary>working example — HTML forms (from https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_forms.asp)</summary><pre><code>&lt;form&gt;
  &lt;label for="fname"&gt;First name:&lt;/label&gt;&lt;br&gt;
  &lt;input type="text" id="fname" name="fname"&gt;&lt;br&gt;
  &lt;label for="lname"&gt;Last name:&lt;/label&gt;&lt;br&gt;
  &lt;input type="text" id="lname" name="lname"&gt;
&lt;/form&gt;</code></pre><ul><li>label for must equal input id to bind them</li><li>every submittable input needs a name attribute or its value is never sent</li><li>one shared radio name means one choice</li><li>form action points at the server-side handler</li></ul></details></p></article>
        <article class="card" data-growth="9" data-seed="5"><h3>Learn track: CSS foundations</h3><p>Start https://www.w3schools.com/css/default.asp — intro https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_intro.asp — syntax https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_syntax.asp — selectors https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_selectors.asp — how-to https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_howto.asp — colors https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_colors.asp — background https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_background.asp — border https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_border.asp — box model https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_boxmodel.asp<details><summary>reference shelf — CSS · Basics (8 of 48)</summary><ul><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/default.asp">default.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_intro.asp">css_intro.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_syntax.asp">css_syntax.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_selectors.asp">css_selectors.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_selectors_grouping.asp">css_selectors_grouping.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_challenges_selectors.asp">css_challenges_selectors.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_howto.asp">css_howto.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_howto_internal.asp">css_howto_internal.asp</a></li></ul></details></p></article>
        <article class="card" data-growth="10" data-seed="6"><h3>Learn track: CSS layout</h3><p>Margin https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_margin.asp — padding https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_padding.asp — display https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_display.asp — position https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_position.asp — align https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_align.asp — flexbox https://www.w3schools.com/css/css3_flexbox.asp — grid https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_grid.asp — responsive https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_rwd_intro.asp<details><summary>reference shelf — CSS · LayoutAndPositioning (8 of 54)</summary><ul><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_display.asp">css_display.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_display_hide.asp">css_display_hide.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_challenges_display.asp">css_challenges_display.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_max-width.asp">css_max-width.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_challenges_max-width.asp">css_challenges_max-width.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_position.asp">css_position.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_positioning_fixed_absolute.asp">css_positioning_fixed_absolute.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_positioning_sticky.asp">css_positioning_sticky.asp</a></li></ul></details></p></article>
        <article class="card" data-growth="11" data-seed="7"><h3>Learn track: CSS motion and modern</h3><p>Transitions https://www.w3schools.com/css/css3_transitions.asp — animations https://www.w3schools.com/css/css3_animations.asp — 2D transforms https://www.w3schools.com/css/css3_2dtransforms.asp — variables https://www.w3schools.com/css/css3_variables.asp — media queries https://www.w3schools.com/css/css3_mediaqueries.asp — fonts https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_font.asp — navbar https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_navbar.asp — tooltip https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_tooltip.asp<details><summary>reference shelf — CSS · Advanced (8 of 119)</summary><ul><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_pseudo_classes.asp">css_pseudo_classes.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_pseudo_classes_interactive.asp">css_pseudo_classes_interactive.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_pseudo_classes_structural.asp">css_pseudo_classes_structural.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_challenges_pseudo_classes.asp">css_challenges_pseudo_classes.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_pseudo_elements.asp">css_pseudo_elements.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_pseudo_elements_text.asp">css_pseudo_elements_text.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_pseudo_elements_content.asp">css_pseudo_elements_content.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_challenges_pseudo_elements.asp">css_challenges_pseudo_elements.asp</a></li></ul></details></p></article>
        <article class="card" data-growth="12" data-seed="8"><h3>Learn track: JavaScript core</h3><p>Start https://www.w3schools.com/js/default.asp — intro https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_intro.asp — syntax https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_syntax.asp — variables https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_variables.asp — functions https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_functions.asp — loops https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_loops.asp — strings https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_strings.asp — arrays https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_arrays.asp — objects https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_objects.asp — quiz https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_quiz.asp — exercises https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_exercises.asp<details><summary>reference shelf — JS · Basics (8 of 39)</summary><ul><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/js/default.asp">default.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_intro.asp">js_intro.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_whereto.asp">js_whereto.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_output.asp">js_output.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_syntax.asp">js_syntax.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_statements.asp">js_statements.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_comments.asp">js_comments.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_variables.asp">js_variables.asp</a></li></ul></details></p></article>
        <article class="card" data-growth="13" data-seed="9"><h3>Learn track: JavaScript advanced</h3><p>Asynchronous https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_asynchronous.asp — async await https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_async_await.asp — classes https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_classes.asp — modules https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_modules.asp — HTML DOM https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_htmldom.asp — events https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_events.asp — fetch API https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_api_fetch.asp — JSON https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_json.asp<details><summary>reference shelf — JS · Advanced (8 of 72)</summary><ul><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_looping.asp">js_looping.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_iterables.asp">js_iterables.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_iterators.asp">js_iterators.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_generators.asp">js_generators.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_math.asp">js_math.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_math_reference.asp">js_math_reference.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_random.asp">js_random.asp</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_regexp.asp">js_regexp.asp</a></li></ul></details></p></article>
        <article class="card" data-growth="14" data-seed="10"><h3>Learn track: React</h3><p>Start https://www.w3schools.com/react/default.asp — intro https://www.w3schools.com/react/react_intro.asp — components https://www.w3schools.com/react/react_components.asp — props https://www.w3schools.com/react/react_props.asp — hooks https://www.w3schools.com/react/react_hooks.asp — useState https://www.w3schools.com/react/react_usestate.asp — useEffect https://www.w3schools.com/react/react_useeffect.asp — router https://www.w3schools.com/react/react_router.asp — quiz https://www.w3schools.com/react/react_quiz.asp — exercises https://www.w3schools.com/react/react_exercises.asp</p></article>
        <article class="card" data-growth="15" data-seed="11"><h3>Learn track: Node.js and TypeScript</h3><p>Node start https://www.w3schools.com/nodejs/default.asp — intro https://www.w3schools.com/nodejs/nodejs_intro.asp — express https://www.w3schools.com/nodejs/nodejs_express.asp — TypeScript https://www.w3schools.com/typescript/index.php — TS intro https://www.w3schools.com/typescript/typescript_intro.php — TS with React https://www.w3schools.com/typescript/typescript_react.php</p></article>
        <article class="card" data-growth="16"><h3>Reference words</h3><p>Each segment opens with one uncompressed 64-bit reference. That single anchor is what breaks the left-to-right dependency chain of classic delta coders.</p></article>
        <article class="card" data-growth="17"><h3>The entropy stage</h3><p>After XOR comes a second pass — zlib in the educational engine, range coding or ANS in a serious one. Two stages: structure first, statistics second.</p></article>
        <article class="card" data-growth="18"><h3>Hooli vs Pied Piper</h3><p>Gavin Belson's Nucleus had the money, the campus, and the keynote. Pied Piper had 8 segments and Jared's unwavering optimism. Guess which one shipped.</p></article>
        <article class="card" data-growth="19"><h3>Gilfoyle's law</h3><p>The mesh stays up because one insomniac Satanist refuses to let it fall. Decentralized routing: no single point of failure, no single point of mercy.</p></article>
        <article class="card" data-growth="20"><h3>Dinesh's crucible</h3><p>Deep loop nests get flattened, leaky mutations get rolled back, latency over 12ms gets rejected. Cleanliness isn't taste — it's a fitness function.</p></article>
        <article class="card" data-growth="21"><h3>Jared's guidance</h3><p>Every pivot survived on Gantt charts and heart. Efficiency isn't just bytes per second; it's keeping the team alive long enough to compress them.</p></article>
        <article class="card" data-growth="22"><h3>Endframe, Bachmanity, Aviato</h3><p>The graveyard of competitors and side quests. Pied Piper outlived them all by doing one impossible thing instead of ten plausible ones.</p></article>
        <article class="card" data-growth="23"><h3>Lossless or it didn't happen</h3><p>decompress(compress(x)) == x, for every x, every time. A single flipped bit is a failed company. The round-trip is the whole religion.</p></article>
        <article class="card" data-growth="24"><h3>The site that makes itself</h3><p>You are reading blocks laid by the maker, one per cycle, through a guardrail that backs up every write. This block is #12 of 12. The repertoire is spent — the page stands as built.</p></article>
